# 📍 Compact Smart GPS Tracker (ESP32-Based)

## 🎯 Product Goal

The goal of this project is to design and develop a **compact, low-power, intelligent GPS tracker** that can:

* 📡 Track location in real-time
* 🌐 Upload data to the internet (WiFi / optional cellular)
* 🏢 Work partially indoors using hybrid positioning (GPS + WiFi)
* 🔋 Achieve long battery life using smart power management
* 🧠 Use motion detection to optimize tracking behavior

---

## 🧩 Key Features

### 📍 Location Tracking

* GPS-based outdoor tracking
* Faster fix using A-GPS support
* Multi-GNSS (GPS, GLONASS, Galileo)

### 🏢 Indoor Support

* WiFi scanning for indoor positioning
* Fallback when GPS signal is weak

### 🔋 Power Optimization

* Deep sleep mode (ESP32)
* Motion-based wakeup using IMU
* Adaptive tracking interval:

  * Moving → frequent updates
  * Stationary → minimal updates

### 🌐 Connectivity

* WiFi-based data upload
* Optional cellular module for remote tracking

### 🚨 Smart Alerts

* Movement detection (anti-theft)
* Low battery alerts
* Device status monitoring

---

## 🧱 Components Required

### 🧠 Microcontroller

* ESP32-C3 Mini Module

  * Low power
  * WiFi + BLE support
  * Compact size

---

### 📍 GPS Module

* u-blox MAX-M10S (Recommended)

  * Low power
  * High sensitivity
  * Fast position fix

---

### 📡 GPS Antenna

* Active Ceramic Patch Antenna (10–25 mm)

  * Better signal reception
  * Works better indoors near windows
  * U.FL connector preferred

---

### 🧭 IMU Sensor

* BMI160 (Recommended) or MPU6050

  * Motion detection
  * Interrupt-based wakeup

---

### 🔋 Power System

* 3.7V LiPo Battery (1000–3000 mAh)
* TP4056 Charging Module
* 3.3V Voltage Regulator (if needed)

---

### 📶 Optional Connectivity (Advanced)

* SIM7070 / SIM7080 (NB-IoT / LTE-M module)

---

### 🔌 Additional Components

* Power switch
* Status LEDs
* Capacitors (decoupling)
* Resistors (pull-up / pull-down)

---

## 🏗️ System Architecture

```
[ GPS Module ] ----\
                    \
                     → [ ESP32-C3 ] → [ WiFi / Cellular ] → Internet (Cloud)
                    /
[ IMU Sensor ] -----/

         ↓
     Battery Power
```

---

## 🔌 Connection Overview

### 📍 GPS → ESP32

* TX → RX
* RX → TX
* VCC → 3.3V
* GND → GND

---

### 🧭 IMU → ESP32 (I2C)

* SDA → GPIO (e.g., GPIO4)
* SCL → GPIO (e.g., GPIO5)
* INT → GPIO (interrupt pin)
* VCC → 3.3V
* GND → GND

---

### 🔋 Power

* Battery → Charging Module → ESP32
* Ensure stable 3.3V supply

---

## ⚙️ Development Process

### 🔹 Phase 1: Prototype

* Connect ESP32 + GPS + IMU
* Read GPS coordinates
* Verify IMU motion detection

---

### 🔹 Phase 2: Connectivity

* Connect to WiFi
* Send GPS data to server (HTTP/MQTT)

---

### 🔹 Phase 3: Power Optimization

* Implement deep sleep
* Use IMU interrupt for wake-up
* Optimize GPS usage (ON only when needed)

---

### 🔹 Phase 4: Intelligence

* Add motion-based tracking logic
* Implement adaptive update intervals
* Add offline data storage

---

### 🔹 Phase 5: Compact Design

* Design custom PCB
* Optimize component placement
* Integrate antenna properly

---

## 🧠 Core Logic (Simplified)

```
IF motion detected:
    Wake ESP32
    Turn ON GPS
    Get location
    Send data to server
    Turn OFF GPS
ELSE:
    Stay in deep sleep
```

---

## 📏 Design Considerations

* Keep antenna facing upward (sky-facing)
* Avoid placing antenna near metal
* Use short RF traces for GPS antenna
* Ensure proper grounding

---

## 🚀 Future Improvements

* Mobile app integration
* Geofencing alerts
* OTA firmware updates
* Enclosure design (waterproof)
* Battery optimization with solar charging

